Z||000000||fotofrank||06-03-99||05:10 PM||||I have a 1984 SE 2M4 with option code WS6-performance package,special. Can anyone tell me what this is?<br>Thanks
Z||000001||SCCA FIERO||06-03-99||06:43 PM||||WS6 consists of stiffer springs and shocks front and rear, 14-in. cast aluminum wheels, and 215/60 Eagle GT tires.
Z||000002||fotofrank||06-03-99||06:55 PM||||OK&gt; SO what is option W69 SE option "special edition"? I thought that this is the stiffer suspention.
Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||06-03-99||07:51 PM||||I have an 86SE V6. I'm not sure but i think the "SE" was a way for Pontiac to carry over the GT without actually calling it the "GT". I think they did this because they knew the "GT" woud come out in late 86. I don't know this for sure it's just a tought.
Z||000004||SCCA FIERO||06-03-99||08:25 PM||||WS9: high mileage coupe(84)<br>what ever that means
Z||000005||Pretender||06-04-99||01:38 AM||||the WS6 option only has 14 inch rims??., so i guess my stock black cross-lace rims automatically exclude me from this option before i go outside and check the options codes?...the new WS6's have it all., 17" chrome, dual ram-air, 326hp,(back seat*sigh*), 13.6 in the 1/4 mile....i don't wanna keep going, but if i don't i'll probably want to buy one..
Z||000006||theogre||06-04-99||07:20 AM||||Acording to the options list I was reading over a while back to decode my sticker,,,,,, If you got the 14" AL wheel <i>as a factory option</i> the heavy duty suspension was "required." <p>The WS6 package included the heavy duty suspension but what else it includes, like wheels, tires, shocks, struts, etc, change over the years. <p>The Hd suspension is included on all SE, GT, and SC's as far as I can tell regardless of it being coded WS6 or not. There are several other codes for it. I can't find my list right now to look them up.
Z||000007||SCCA FIERO||06-04-99||12:45 PM||||Here are the list of codes: http://www.fiero.mn.org/knowledge/features/option.htm
Z||000008||theogre||06-04-99||01:13 PM||||Ah, there it is,,,,, My 87SC has the y99 suspension package wich required the n78 wheel....... I had it backwards.<p>If the WS6 package is/was any better than what I have it can't be by a whole lot. God this thing is stiff. So far the only 2 times I've broken it loose are once in the snow, and once when i first got it and over breaked into a U turn. In the U all it did was push. In the snow the ass came loose and snapped out about 3 times before the tires bit again.<p>Right now all I need to do to it is figure out what tires I'm going to use next. These are about gone. But then when you average around 25-30K miles a year, tires don't last too long.
Z||000009||grizco||06-08-99||05:17 PM||||I've never had mine turn a complete circle in the snow. (up here in Alaska we get plenty of it) I've had it turn side ways a couple of times but it usually pulls out of it.
Z||000010||Carrolles||06-09-99||07:14 AM||||I've never had mine break loose in the snow.<p>Of course I do live in Birmingham, Alabama.
Z||000011||theogre||06-09-99||07:29 AM||||i didn't spin...... hit one of those slush piles in the middle of the road while pulling out and fished it pretty far..... it cam back around, but it likely would have spun on allot of people. It was pretty sideways for around 75 feet before I got a bite into something solid.<p>And I was off above.... I've got the F41 Hd suspension package, not Y99. It's still stiff as hell tho. You have to hit a speed bump realy hard to push it to the stops.
Z||000012||lowCG||06-09-99||06:16 PM||||All the Fiero's I've seen come with progressive rate spring(rear)that sucks pretty bad,even the base,four cyl.cars start out soft and wallow,then as you get into the spring,get way stiffer.There's only a small portion of the travel that isn't too soft or way too stiff.Finally got sick of the poor engineering and found some springs that work.<br>Fronts are almost as wierd,but in a different way(wrong frequncy).
Z||000013||Haze_Performance||04-19-2000||03:47 AM||||Sorry about posting something that is so old ....but I was wondering because my 85 2M4 came stock with 14" Alu. wheels...so does that mean it has the WS6 susp.??  ||||reg||6
Z||000014||theogre||04-19-2000||09:46 AM||||no. check the RPO sticker. It may have one of the other handling packages. WS6 is/was a "tuned" setup, which really doesn't mean anything any more becuase the original shocks and struts are worn out or have already been replaced.<P>All SE, all GT, most likely all SC, have an upgraded suspension. The base ones could be ordered with it. F41, and Y99, are other RPOs for the upgraded suspension.||||reg||1
